            <ArticleTitle>[Central electroanalgesia in arresting the acute pain-ischemic syndrome at the prehospital stage].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>81-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Central electroanalgesia (EA) was used by the first aid team in 70 patients with angina pectoris and myocardial infarction for arresting the pain syndrome. The apparatus &quot;Electronarcon&quot; and &quot;LENAR&quot; were applied. The efficacy of EA was observed in residual pains 25-40 min after administration of narcotics as well as in combination of small doses of phentanyl (0.025-0.5 mg) and EA. The use of EA allows application of small doses of narcotics to exclude the respiration arrest and prolong the analgesic effect up to 150 min. It is recommended to use EA in the combined treatment of acute coronary insufficiency at the prehospital stage.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
